

-------COLCON BUILD----------------------------------------------------

- colcon build (you use this command in the project folder)
  (when making a new project in the project folder type this)
  (make a src folder before/after typing this command)
  (you use this command every time you make a change in the code or make a new file/folder)
  
  **** Recommended
- colcon build --packages-select packageName --symlink-install
	(makes it so that you don't have to run the build command every time you change something)
	(you still need to run it if you made a new file/folder)
	**** use this for bigger projects it would take a long time to build everything

	***** Recommended
-	colcon build --packages-select packageName
	(if you want to update a specific package)
	*****


-------GEDIT SOURCE----------------------------------------------------

- gedit ~/.bashrc (opnes txt editor when ran)
	(paste "source ~/project_name/install/setup.bash" at the bottom)
	(it makes it so that ubuntu sees the project)
	
	
- source install/setup.bash (you could also use this command)
  


-------PACKAGE CREATION------------------------------------------------

- ros2 pkg create projName_codeLang_pkg --build-type ament_python --dependencies rclpy
	(creates the package. research before using)
	(this is for python packages)
	
	
- ros2 pkg create projName_interfaces
	(this creates a project folder for the interface)
	(you mainly do it as a sub folder not the main one)



-------SOURCE----------------------------------------------------------

- source ~/.bashrc
	(if the program is not loading after you ran colcon build --packages-select packageName nodeName --symlink-install)
	(for me it just fixed it self after a while it works on newly opened terminals)



-------RUN-------------------------------------------------------------

- ros2 run packageName nodeName (just the nodeName no .py)
  (runs your program)
  
  
  *********
  (you can either type -r for remap or --remap, also -p for parameter or --parameter)

- ros2 run packageName nodeName --ros-args --remap __node:=node_new_name
  (this changes the node name that is run)
  (it helps when you are running multiple of the same nodes)


- ros2 run packageName nodeName --ros-args -r serverName:=newServerName
	(this changes the server name that is run)
	(it helps when you are running multiple of the same servers)
	
- ros2 run packageName nodeName --ros-args -p parameterName:=anything (ex. anything = value/string)
	(this changes the server name that is run)
	(it helps when you are running multiple of the same servers)

  *********
  
  

