-------NODE------------------------------------------------------------

- ros2 node list
	(shows a list of the nodes that are running)

- ros2 node info /nodeName
	(shows the channels for the node)
	(the node needs to be running)



-------TOPIC-----------------------------------------------------------

- ros2 topic list
	(lists the topics that have been published)
	(to publish a topic you need to start a node and have this line in it)
	(elf.create_publisher check rosCode for how this works line 6)
	
- ros2 topic echo channelName
	(you get the channel name from ros2 topic list)
	(this shows you what the topic is sending)

- ros2 topci info channelName
	(this gives you the specifics of the channel)
	(it helps when you need to know the position of somethin)
	
	(check turtlesim_ws/turtlesim_py_pkg/turtlesim_py_pkg/pathfinder)
	(for the libraries we have "from turtlesim.msg import Pose)
	(we found this in the info type. the dot is a slash '/' in python)



-------PARAM-----------------------------------------------------------

- ros2 param list (lists the parameters that are available)

- ros2 param get /nodeName parameterName
	(you get the nodeName and the parameter from the param list)
	(the paramters are the ones under the nodeName)



-------RQT-------------------------------------------------------------

- rqt
	(after selecting Plugins, Introspection and Node Graph)
	(you can see the nodes that are running at the moment)
	(you might need to refresh the page to see them)
	
- rqt_graph
	(rather than navigating to the node graph it just starts there)



